 r"I am writing to apply for the Networks AI \& Data Science Professional role in BT Group's Networks Data \& AI team. I completed an MSc in Health Data Science at University College London in September 2026, where a distinction is expected, after a BSc in Biological Sciences at Imperial College London, and I currently work as a Data Analyst Intern at TikTok Shop UK. Across my academic and professional experience I have analysed very large datasets, built machine learning and generative AI solutions, and turned them into products and insights that people use to make decisions.",

 r"What attracts me most to this role is that the work has a visible end point: fixed and mobile networks that are monitored, maintained and invested in more intelligently, so that millions of customers get a better everyday experience. Building data products for predictive maintenance and network investment, alongside data and AI engineers and product owners, is exactly the kind of applied data science I want to do. I enjoy taking an unclear business need, understanding what the people who own it actually require, and turning it into a solution that can be tested and improved.",

 r"My MSc dissertation applied machine learning to 458,840 UK Biobank participants. I compared logistic regression with three tree ensembles for risk prediction and checked calibration as well as accuracy, then used doubly robust causal forests on 71,428 participants to estimate the effect of 24 lifestyle transitions, with sensitivity analyses for unmeasured confounding. I delivered the results as an interactive Streamlit tool so that non-specialists could explore them.",

 r"At DS Digital Technology I worked as a Data Scientist Intern on a patient-facing AI product for a pharmaceutical client. I built a Python pipeline that called six LLM APIs with retrieval augmentation and scored more than 2,400 responses against a 246-question benchmark the client adopted as its acceptance standard, and designed blinded A/B tests to measure whether a knowledge-graph feature genuinely improved answer quality. This taught me to define how value will be measured before deploying generative AI.",

 r"At TikTok Shop UK I analyse merchant and transaction data in SQL and Python and build the KPI frameworks and dashboards that operations, product and commercial teams use to set targets and track initiatives. When my supervisor asked me to configure a merchant campaign by hand, I used Claude Code to build an AI agent with a validation step to check its accuracy, which cut the time the task took by around 40 to 50 percent.",

 r"I would bring BT strong Python, SQL and statistics, hands-on machine learning and LLM experience, and the ability to explain complex findings clearly to technical and non-technical stakeholders. I have the right to work in the UK until January 2029, and I am based in London and happy to work from the London office.",

 r"Thank you for considering my application. I would welcome the opportunity to discuss how my experience in data science and AI could contribute to the Networks Data \& AI team.",
